# E-RAKSHAK — local configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and fill in your key. `.env` is
# gitignored; this example file is not, so never put a real key in here.

# ── Investigation Copilot (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables the AI case summary and Q&A panel. Everything else in the platform —
# ingestion, entity resolution, the seven rules, scoring, the graphs, the
# forensic report and the STR — runs without it. Leave this unset and the
# copilot panel simply shows a "not connected" state.
#
# Get a free key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to gemini-2.5-flash, falling back to gemini-2.0-flash and
# then gemini-flash-latest if the key cannot reach the first choice.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ── Durable artefact storage (optional, but required for hosted deployments) ──
# Archives forensic reports, STRs and ingested evidence to Supabase Storage.
#
# Leave unset for local workstation use: everything is written to disk under
# backend/reports/ and backend/data/uploaded/ exactly as before.
#
# Set these when hosting. On Heroku, Railway, Render, Fly, Lambda or any
# container without a mounted volume the filesystem is EPHEMERAL — every
# generated .docx is destroyed on the next restart or redeploy. With these set,
# reports upload to private buckets and download via short-lived signed URLs.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com
#   2. Project Settings -> API for the URL, and the SECRET (service_role) key
#   3. Run backend/storage/supabase_schema.sql in the SQL editor (optional —
#      adds a queryable audit index; storage works without it)
#
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is service-role: it bypasses Row Level Security. Keep it
# server-side only. Never put it in frontend code or commit it. The publishable
# key is NOT used by this backend and is not read here.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
